milton, Ontario, when he was 17 years old, in 1899.  By 1907, he was the greatest Canadian sprinter to date, winning over 40 events in that year alone."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The two fastest heat winners were Kerr (22.2) and the American " [:a {:href "/athletes/78507"} "Frank Hamilton"] " (22.4).  Both runners were drawn in the same heat in the semi-finals, where Kerr was the winner in a close race and Hamilton was eliminated.  Kerr went on to win the final and, with the South African " [:a {:href "/athletes/75343"} "Reggie Walker"] " winning the " [:a {:href "/results/56265"} "100 metres"] ", the United States failed to win either sprint for the first time.  This is a relatively rare occurrence at the Olympics and, as of 2024, has only been repeated in " [:a {:href "/editions/9/sports/ATH"} "1928"] ", " [:a {:href "/editions/15/sports/ATH"} "1960"] ", " [:a {:href "/editions/18/sports/ATH"} "1972"] ", " [:a {:href "/editions/19/sports/ATH"} "1976"] ", and " [:a {:href "/editions/20/sports/ATH"} "1980"] "."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/66116"} "Bobby Kerr"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} "22.2 (1 h11)"] [:td {} "22.6 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "22.6 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78236"} "Bobby Cloughen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "23.4 (1 h8)"] [:td {} "22.6 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "22.6est / at 2 feet (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver